IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wsa-charges`

-- Water Services Act 2012 (WA), Part 5 (water service charges) -- worked cases, from the seat of the property owner.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked against
-- a decided case, a water bill, the regulations under the Act or the code of conduct (none deposited). Amounts of charges,
-- interest and fees are ILLUSTRATIVE inputs.
--
-- Generated by the scratchpad script gen_wa_water-services-act-2012_baseline.py. Expected results were written by hand from the text.
--
-- The life. c055 (2029-07-15): Chloe and Liam take handover of their new house in Byford and live in it; the lot was
-- bought vacant (settled 15 May 2028). "Who levies what on a new house?" -- here, the water charges.

§ `s 73 -- the owner's entitlement to the service`

-- c055: Chloe and Liam, owners of the Byford house, statutory charges applying, nothing overdue (s 73(1))
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to the water service` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- s 73(2)(b): the entitlement is subject to the charges due being paid
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to the water service` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- a tenant is not the owner: s 73 gives the entitlement to the owner
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to the water service` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

§ `s 124(2)(c) -- charges before connection`

-- c055: the Byford lot before the house is connected, the sewer main at the boundary, the regulations applying the charge to unconnected land (s 124(2)(c)(i))
#ASSERT `Can I be charged for a service I am not connected to` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- without a regulation applying the charge to unconnected land, s 124(2)(c) does nothing by itself
#ASSERT `Can I be charged for a service I am not connected to` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

§ `s 126(1) -- unpaid charges follow the land`

-- c055 variant: statutory charges left unpaid on the lot before Chloe and Liam bought it
#ASSERT `Can the unpaid charges on my land be recovered from me as owner` `a statutory water service charge` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- s 126(1) names alternative charges under s 75(2)(c)
#ASSERT `Can the unpaid charges on my land be recovered from me as owner` `an alternative charge under an agreement in place of a statutory charge` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- s 75(2)(b) charges are not named in s 126(1)
#ASSERT `Can the unpaid charges on my land be recovered from me as owner` `a charge under an agreement where no statutory charge applies` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- s 126(1) reaches only the owner for the time being
#ASSERT `Can the unpaid charges on my land be recovered from me as owner` `a statutory water service charge` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `ss 124(2)(d), 125, 126 -- owner or tenant`

-- c055: a detached house on its own connection, no regulation making a user liable
#ASSERT `Who is liable for the water charges on my home` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the owner only`
-- s 124(2)(d): the house let, the regulations making the measured user liable
#ASSERT `Who is liable for the water charges on my home` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the owner, and the tenant to the extent the regulations make a measured user liable`
-- s 125(1): 2 or more dwellings on a single property connection, the licensee apportioning
#ASSERT `Who is liable for the water charges on my home` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `each owner or occupier for the share the licensee apportioned`

-- s 126(1): recoverable from the owner for the time being while unpaid (inference, labelled in the module)
#ASSERT `Can the charges still be recovered from me if my tenant does not pay` TRUE EQUALS TRUE

§ `s 76 -- the previous owner's agreement`

-- s 76(4)(c): charges terms bind a later owner whether or not they had notice
#ASSERT `Am I bound by the previous owner's agreement` `a term about water service charges` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- s 76(3), (7): registered only 10 days before possession, so no deemed prior notice
#ASSERT `Am I bound by the previous owner's agreement` `any other term` 10 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- s 76(3), (6), (7): registered at least 21 days before possession
#ASSERT `Am I bound by the previous owner's agreement` `any other term` 30 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE

§ `s 128 -- memorial on the title`

-- s 128(2)(a)
#ASSERT `Can the licensee lodge a memorial on my title` `statutory or alternative water service charges in arrears` EQUALS TRUE
-- nothing in arrears: no memorial
#ASSERT `Can the licensee lodge a memorial on my title` `nothing, or something else` EQUALS FALSE

-- s 128(3): a transfer lodged after the memorial, without the licensee's written consent
#ASSERT `Can my dealing be registered despite a memorial` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- s 128(3): with the licensee's written consent
#ASSERT `Can my dealing be registered despite a memorial` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE

-- s 128(4): the arrears paid
#ASSERT `Must the licensee withdraw the memorial` TRUE EQUALS TRUE

§ `s 124(2)(n) -- late payment`

-- illustrative: a $400 bill with $6 of interest under the regulations, no penalty
#ASSERT `How much do I owe on an overdue bill` 400 6 0 EQUALS 406

§ `s 95 -- cutting off or reducing the supply`

-- c055 variant: Chloe and Liam 45 days overdue, living in the house: s 95(1)(b) ground, but s 95(3) bars cutting off
#ASSERT `Can my water be cut off or reduced` 45 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `its flow may be reduced, but it cannot be cut off without the occupier's agreement`
-- 29 days overdue: not yet 30 days after falling due
#ASSERT `Can my water be cut off or reduced` 29 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `neither`
-- s 95(3): the occupier agrees
#ASSERT `Can my water be cut off or reduced` 45 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `it may be cut off or its flow reduced`
-- s 95(1)(a): unoccupied land, no dwelling
#ASSERT `Can my water be cut off or reduced` 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `it may be cut off or its flow reduced`
-- s 95(2): waste only
#ASSERT `Can my water be cut off or reduced` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `its flow may be reduced, if the licensee is satisfied that is necessary to prevent waste`
-- s 95(4): the licence restricts it
#ASSERT `Can my water be cut off or reduced` 45 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `neither`

-- s 95(6)(a)
#ASSERT `Does being cut off end what I owe`  EQUALS FALSE

-- s 95(7)(a): the arrears with interest plus an illustrative $50 of prescribed fees
#ASSERT `What must I pay before my water is restored` 406 50 FALSE EQUALS 456
-- s 95(7)(b): an arrangement the licensee is satisfied with instead
#ASSERT `What must I pay before my water is restored` 406 50 TRUE EQUALS 0

§ `s 77 -- interruptions`

-- s 77(2): an emergency shutdown, no negligence, bad faith or agreement
#ASSERT `Can I claim for loss from an interruption` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- s 77(2)(a)(i): negligence
#ASSERT `Can I claim for loss from an interruption` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE

§ `ss 79, 129 -- the meter`

-- s 79(1): no evidence to the contrary
#ASSERT `Is my meter presumed correct` FALSE EQUALS TRUE

-- s 129(2): meter reading needs no notice
#ASSERT `How many hours notice must I get before entry` `to read the meter` FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0
-- s 129(5): disruptive routine work
#ASSERT `How many hours notice must I get before entry` `for routine inspection or maintenance` TRUE FALSE EQUALS 48

§ `ss 68, 69 -- the ombudsman`

-- c055: Chloe and Liam are customers of the licensee (s 3(1), s 68(1)(a))
#ASSERT `Can I take my dispute to the water ombudsman` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- s 69(2)(a): already before a court or tribunal
#ASSERT `Can I take my dispute to the water ombudsman` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- s 68(1)(b): a neighbour affected by the licensee's service
#ASSERT `Can I take my dispute to the water ombudsman` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE

